    "@value" : "ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/BoundaryDistinctness",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Boundary distinctness refers to the clarity or sharpness of the boundary between two soil horizons. It is classified based on the thickness of the transitional zone and helps determine soil formation processes. Source: Soil Survey Staff (2014). Keys to Soil Taxonomy."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "BoundaryDistinctness"
