  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "CEC is the soil’s ability to hold and exchange cations (positively charged ions) such as calcium, magnesium, potassium, and sodium. It is a critical property for soil fertility and nutrient retention. Source: Sparks, D.L. (2003). Environmental Soil Chemistry."
  } ],
