    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Specialization for GloSIS of the ISO 28258 Horizon soil feature type, defined as the domain of a soil with a certain vertical extension, which is more or less parallel to the surface and is homogeneous for most morphological and analytical characteristics, developed in a parent material through pedogenic processes or made up of in situ sedimented organic residues of up-growing plants (peat)"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "GL_Horizon"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://w3id.org/glosis/model/iso28258/2013/Horizon"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid335"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid336"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid337"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid338"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Data model for the Global Soil Information System (GloSIS) v1.0, edited by Tomas Reznik and Katharina Schleidt"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Specialization for GloSIS of the ISO 28258 Layer soil feature type, defined as the domain of a soil with a certain vertical extension developed through non-pedogenic processes, displaying an unconformity to possibly over- or underlying adjacent domains"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "GL_Layer"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://w3id.org/glosis/model/iso28258/2013/Layer"
  }, {
