  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Mottle abundance refers to the quantity of color variations or mottling in a soil horizon, often indicating fluctuating water conditions or redox processes. Source: Soil Survey Manual (USDA, 2017)."
