  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Extractable potassium is the portion of potassium in the soil solution or loosely bound to particles that can be removed by chemical extractants and absorbed by plants. Source: Brady, N.C., & Weil, R.R. (2008). The Nature and Properties of Soils."
  } ],
