    "@value" : "Exchangeable sodium refers to sodium ions held on soil colloid surfaces. High exchangeable sodium can cause soil dispersion, leading to poor structure and reduced permeability. Source: Richards, L.A. (1954). Diagnosis and Improvement of Saline and Alkali Soils."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
