  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Soluble anions total refers to the total concentration of negatively charged ions, such as chloride, sulfate, and bicarbonate, in the soil solution. These influence soil salinity and alkalinity. Source: Sparks, D.L. (2003). Environmental Soil Chemistry."
