  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Soluble cations total measures the sum of positively charged ions (e.g., sodium, calcium, magnesium, potassium) dissolved in soil solution. These affect soil salinity and nutrient availability. Source: Richards, L.A. (1954). Diagnosis and Improvement of Saline and Alkali Soils."
