    "@value" : "Extractable sulfur refers to the sulfur present in a readily available form for plants, typically measured using chemical extractants. It includes forms such as sulfate sulfur, which is essential for plant nutrition. Source: Brady, N.C., & Weil, R.R. (2008). The Nature and Properties of Soils."
  } ],
